{
 "$schema": "bloom-levels/2",
 "version": 2,
 "description": "Pikmin Bloom level-up requirements. Each entry is what must be done WHILE AT level-1 to REACH that level. 'steps' and 'flowers' are per-level amounts. 'cumulativeSteps' (levels 3-100) is the lifetime total the game asks for ('Walk a total of X steps').",
 "sourceUrl": "https://www.pikminwiki.com/Level",
 "retrieved": "2026-11-04",
 "maxLevel": 130,
 "rules": {
  "stepsCarryOver": "Levels 3-100 use a lifetime step total, so extra steps count toward the next level. From level 101 the task is 'Walk X steps' at that level: extra steps do NOT carry over (confirmed by players on the official Pikmin Bloom support forum, 2026-01, and consistent with the game).",
  "flowersCarryOver": "Never. Every 'Plant X flowers' task counts only flowers planted while at that level."
 },
 "notes": [
  "Levels 1-100: checked row by row against the wiki on 2026-11-04 (steps, lifetime totals, flowers, tasks). All match.",
  "Level 111: verified in the game (Lv 110 profile shows Walk 479,200 steps / Plant 294,900 flowers).",
  "Levels 113-123: the wiki lists these one row early. Its rows 110 and 112-122 were added by players recording what their profile showed AT that level, which is the requirement for the NEXT level. This file shifts them to the level they unlock. The wiki's row 111 (479,300) was a +500/+300 guess and is not used.",
  "Levels 110, 112 and 124-130 are estimates from a single growth model that reproduces every observed 101+ value: requirement(L) = floor100(base x 1.0009875^(L-101)), base 474,577 steps / 292,069 flowers. It matches all 21 flower values exactly and all step values within 100.",
  "The level cap rose from 100 to 130 on 2025-05-12 (wiki, citing @PikminBloom).",
  "The app lets the user override any level with what the game actually shows."
 ],
